```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I didn't add the `http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The fetch would send the full reply text in a GET query string to an external host on every call. That leaks user-session content, and URLs are commonly logged. It also goes beyond this node's `with` clause, which grants only `response-channel`. If the platform team wants enrichment, I can add it if the grant is recorded in the node's `with` clause and the request carries a non-sensitive key or a hash rather than the raw text.

